* soft-start-loop-gain -- Tian dual-injection loop-gain testbench for the LDO
* main loop with design/ldo_softstart.sch's FB-injection element IN the loop,
* at PINNED points of the soft-start ramp (issue #196).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* What this deck is, and what it is not
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* This is sim/loop-stability/testbench/tb_loop_stability.spice.in's deck --
* same DUT cell, same break point, same Tian/Middlebrook dual injection, same
* margin and gain-resurgence extraction idioms, same AC band and resolution --
* with exactly one thing added: the soft-start ramp node SSR is brought out as
* a port and PINNED, so a state the ramp only passes THROUGH in a transient
* can be held still and measured in the frequency domain.
*
* Read the loop-stability deck for the derivations this one inherits verbatim:
*   - why the loop is broken at ERRAMP_OUT -> PASS_GATE (two deliberately
*     unconnected ports of design/ldo_core.sch),
*   - why plain series-voltage injection is not accurate at this break and
*     T = (Tv*Ti - 1)/(Tv + Ti + 2) is,
*   - what phase margin / gain margin / resurgence_db mean here (DR-0001's
*     45 deg / 10 dB bars and DR-0008's precondition check, issue #59),
*   - why the resurgence scan starts a FIXED 5% above the first 0 dB crossing
*     (issue #69) and why AC_DEC is 400 (issue #58),
*   - why the ideal-current-source load is the conservative stability model,
*   - why Dclamp is present and why it is inert at the operating point.
* None of that is restated here; sim/soft-start-loop-gain/README.md says which
* pieces are inherited and which are new.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Why SSR has to be pinned, and what pinning it costs
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* design/ldo_softstart.sch ramps its internal node SSR from 0 V to above VREF
* over milliseconds (Fss_ramp charging Css), and the FB-injection element it
* drives is what holds the output down during that ramp. Every state of the
* hand-over -- injection fully on, injection about to rectify off, injection
* just off -- is therefore a TRANSIENT state, and a small-signal margin is a
* statement about a fixed operating point. The only way to ask "what is the
* loop's phase margin DURING the hand-over" is to hold the ramp still.
*
* SSR is a legitimate node to hold still, because nothing in the main loop
* drives it: its only connections are Fss_ramp (a CCCS referred to VREF, an
* ideal deck-level source here), Css to VSS, Mdis_ss's drain (off while
* enabled), Mtop_ss's source (the ramp ceiling clamp) and Mgma_ss's GATE. The
* loop reaches SSR only through Mgma_ss's and Mtop_ss's own overlap
* capacitance, into Css (a 60u x 60u mim cap, ~7 pF) -- three orders of
* magnitude larger -- so the node is already an AC ground in the real circuit.
* Pinning it with an ideal source makes it exactly one.
*
* That claim is not left as prose: sweep.py runs one deck per PVT point with
* the SSR port brought out and NOT pinned, which is electrically identical to
* the unmodified design netlist, and its margins are compared point for point
* against sim/loop-stability/'s own record. See the "anchor" phase in
* sweep.py and the record's cross-check section.
*
* The SSR port itself is added by sweep.py, mechanically, to a COPY of
* design/netlist/ldo_core.spice: one port name appended to two `.subckt` lines
* and one instance line, nothing else. SSR is already a node of the cell, so
* naming it in the port list renames nothing and connects nothing --
* selftest.py asserts the transform is exactly that, and the unpinned deck
* above measures that it is.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Load model
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Both a resistive load and an ideal current sink are instantiated; sweep.py
* enables one and parks the other (RLOAD = 1e12 ohm, or ILOAD = 0). Which one
* is used is part of the operating point and is reported in every ROW line:
*
*   - LOW on the ramp the load MUST be resistive. The soft-start mechanism
*     works by injecting a current into FB, which forces the regulated output
*     to VOUT = 1.5 * V(SSR) (FB = VREF and the 300k/600k divider); at the
*     bottom of the ramp that is a fraction of a volt, and an ideal sink
*     demanding the rated 50 mA from a 0.1 V output has no solution on the
*     regulating branch at all. A 36 ohm resistor is what the rated load
*     physically is (1.8 V / 50 mA) and it tracks the ramp, exactly as
*     sim/soft-start/testbench/tb_soft_start.spice.in models it.
*   - AT AND ABOVE the hand-over the ideal sink is used as well, because that
*     is the model every sim/loop-stability record uses, and a margin measured
*     against a different load model is not comparable with them. A resistive
*     load adds 1/Rload of damping in parallel with the output pole and
*     flatters the result; the sink is the conservative choice.
*
* Template: the at-sign-delimited placeholders are substituted by sweep.py
* (PDK paths, corner sections, temperature, supply, the instrumented netlist,
* the SSR pin and its list of values, and the load/output-network lists)
* before the deck is handed to `ngspice -b`.

.include "@DESIGN_INCLUDE@"
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MOS_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @RES_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @BJT_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @DIODE_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MOSCAP_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MIMCAP_CORNER@

.temp @TEMP_C@

* --- model binning is per-FINGER, and that has to be said out loud ---------
* gf180mcu's device models are binned, and the widest bin any of them has is
* W <= 100.01 um (sm141064.ngspice's `wmax`). design/ldo_core.sch's pass
* device is `W=2000u nf=40` -- 2 mm of total width in 40 fingers of 50 um --
* so the bin it belongs in exists only if the binning divides W by nf.
*
* Whether ngspice does that is NOT a property of the netlist or the PDK: it
* is ngspice's `wnflag` (src/spicelib/parser/inpgmod.c), which defaults to 1
* only in HSPICE/Spectre compatibility mode and to 0 otherwise. On a host
* whose ngspice starts with "No compatibility mode selected!" and no
* `wnflag` in `spinit`/`.spiceinit`, EVERY deck in this repo that
* instantiates the pass device dies at parse time with
*
*     could not find a valid modelname
*
* -- which is one of sim/harness/runner.py's FATAL_LOG_PATTERNS, so it is
* correctly reported as a failure rather than silently mis-simulated. Setting
* it here makes this deck give the same answer on both kinds of host instead
* of depending on the host's ngspice startup files, which no record captures.
* Verified on the host that produced this experiment's first record: with
* this line, `sim/loop-stability/`'s own deck reproduces its committed record
* `20260906-071437-fff0bf0` at tt/27C/3.30V/50mA/1uF/1mohm to within
* 0.22 deg PM and 0.15 dB GM (the cross-invocation budget #182/#185
* established is ~2 deg / ~1 dB), i.e. this setting is what that record was
* taken under. See sim/soft-start-loop-gain/README.md's "Model binning"
* section and the follow-up issue filed for the other benches.
.options wnflag=1

* The SSR-instrumented copy of design/netlist/ldo_core.spice for this DUT
* variant -- see sweep.py's instrument_core() and the header above.
.include "@LDO_NETLIST@"

* --- stimulus ------------------------------------------------------------
Vin VIN 0 DC @VIN_V@
Ven EN 0 DC @VIN_V@

* --- reference (issue #174 / DR-0021) ------------------------------------
* Identical to the loop-stability and soft-start decks: VREF is a top-level
* port of ldo_core, driven here by the same ideal 1.2 V source those decks
* use, standing in for a bandgap block that does not exist yet.
Vref VREF 0 DC 1.2

* --- DUT, loop broken at ERRAMP_OUT -> PASS_GATE --------------------------
* Port order: VIN VOUT EN VSS ERRAMP_OUT PASS_GATE VREF, plus the SSR port
* sweep.py adds.
Xdut VIN VOUT EN 0 AINJ BINJ VREF SSRPIN ldo_core

* --- soft-start ramp node ------------------------------------------------
* Either an ideal source pinning SSR at the operating point under test, or
* nothing at all (the "anchor" phase, where SSR settles where the design puts
* it and the deck is electrically the loop-stability deck).
@SSR_SOURCE@

* --- Tian dual-injection network -----------------------------------------
* Vinj is a DC short: the operating point is the true closed-loop one.
Vinj AINJ BINJ DC 0 AC 0
Iinj 0 BINJ DC 0 AC 0

* --- load + output network (swept below; these are the initial values) ----
Iload VOUT 0 DC @ILOAD@
Rload VOUT NLD @RLOAD@
Vlmeas NLD 0 DC 0
Resr VOUT NESR 0.001
Cout NESR 0 1e-6

* --- removing the non-physical DC branch ----------------------------------
* Inherited verbatim from tb_loop_stability.spice.in, including the measured
* evidence that it is inert at the operating point (reverse-biased by the
* output voltage, cjo=0 tt=0 so it adds no AC capacitance at all). It matters
* less here than there -- the resistive-load phases bound VOUT from below on
* their own -- but the ideal-sink phases have exactly the unbounded-VOUT
* branch it exists to deny, so it stays.
.model dclamp d(is=1e-14 cjo=0 tt=0 n=1 rs=0)
Dclamp 0 VOUT dclamp

* DC branch seed, empty unless sweep.py is retrying this corner -- see
* dc_seed_lines() in sweep.py.
@DC_SEED@

.control
set noaskquit

echo "* corner_id=@CORNER_ID@ corner=@CORNER_NAME@ temp_c=@TEMP_C@ vin_v=@VIN_V@"
echo "* phase=@PHASE@ variant=@VARIANT@ iload_a=@ILOAD@ rload_ohm=@RLOAD@"
echo "* ac sweep: dec @AC_DEC@ @F_START@ @F_STOP@ ; Tian dual injection at ERRAMP_OUT->PASS_GATE"
echo "* columns: ROW ssr_cmd= ssr_v= fb_v= vout_v= isup_a= ceff_f= esr_ohm="
echo "*          dcgain_db= f0_hz= phase_at_f0_deg= f180_hz= gain_at_f180_db="
echo "*          f0_rising_hz= resurgence_db="
echo "* (phase margin = 180 + phase_at_f0_deg ; gain margin = -gain_at_f180_db ;"
echo "*  resurgence_db = max |T| in dB above the first 0 dB crossing, DR-0008 ;"
echo "*  an empty f180/gain field means the phase never reaches -180 deg in band ;"
echo "*  ssr_cmd is what this deck COMMANDED the ramp node to, or 'free' when it"
echo "*  is not pinned; ssr_v/fb_v/vout_v are what the DC solve LANDED on)"
echo "* Fields are written key=value BECAUSE a failed meas leaves its value"
echo "* empty: with bare positional fields an empty one vanishes into the"
echo "* whitespace and every field after it is read as the wrong quantity."

foreach ss @SSR_LIST@
  @SSR_ALTER@
  foreach ce @CEFF_LIST@
    foreach es @ESR_LIST@
      destroy all
      alter Cout = $ce
      alter Resr = $es

      * ---- DC operating point (closed loop; Vinj is a DC short) ----------
      * Three landed quantities, not one. VOUT alone cannot tell the intended
      * soft-start branch from a clamp latch low on the ramp, because low on
      * the ramp the INTENDED VOUT is itself near zero. FB is what
      * discriminates: the whole soft-start mechanism is "hold FB at VREF with
      * an injected current and let the divider set VOUT", so FB ~ VREF is the
      * signature of the branch this experiment is about, at every point of
      * the ramp. sweep.py checks both, plus VOUT against 1.5*V(SSR).
      op
      let vout_dc = v(vout)
      let fb_dc = v(xdut.fb)
      let ssr_dc = v(ssrpin)
      let isup_dc = -i(vin)
      set vout_str = "$&vout_dc"
      set fb_str = "$&fb_dc"
      set ssr_str = "$&ssr_dc"
      set isup_str = "$&isup_dc"

      * ---- voltage injection --------------------------------------------
      alter @Vinj[acmag] = 1
      alter @Iinj[acmag] = 0
      ac dec @AC_DEC@ @F_START@ @F_STOP@
      let tv = -v(ainj)/v(binj)
      set vplot = $curplot

      * ---- current injection --------------------------------------------
      alter @Vinj[acmag] = 0
      alter @Iinj[acmag] = 1
      ac dec @AC_DEC@ @F_START@ @F_STOP@
      let ti = -i(vinj)/(i(vinj)+1)
      let tvv = {$vplot}.tv

      * ---- Tian loop gain, magnitude and unwrapped phase -----------------
      let t = (tvv*ti - 1)/(tvv + ti + 2)
      let tdb = db(t)
      let tph = 180*cph(t)/pi

      * ---- margins -------------------------------------------------------
      meas ac dcg find tdb at=@F_START@
      meas ac f0 when tdb=0 fall=1
      meas ac phx find tph when tdb=0 fall=1
      meas ac f180 when tph=-180 fall=1
      meas ac gmx find tdb when tph=-180 fall=1
      meas ac f0r when tdb=0 rise=1

      * ---- gain resurgence above the first 0 dB crossing (#59, DR-0008) ---
      let fres = f0*1.05
      meas ac tres max tdb from=$&fres to=@F_STOP@

      echo "ROW ssr_cmd=$ss ssr_v=$ssr_str fb_v=$fb_str vout_v=$vout_str isup_a=$isup_str ceff_f=$ce esr_ohm=$es dcgain_db=$&dcg f0_hz=$&f0 phase_at_f0_deg=$&phx f180_hz=$&f180 gain_at_f180_db=$&gmx f0_rising_hz=$&f0r resurgence_db=$&tres"
    end
  end
end
echo "* SWEEP COMPLETE @CORNER_ID@"
.endc
.end
